      "chunk_id": "sha256:7e18c7e0f64d74a9396febd331e24a9f7b333170af2bb72bd837c16db266cd4e",
      "quote": "To prevent data leakage, it is good practice to split your data into train and test subsets first . Feature selection can then be formed using just the train dataset. Notice that whenever we use fit or fit_transform , we only use the train dataset."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "sha256:7e18c7e0f64d74a9396febd331e24a9f7b333170af2bb72bd837c16db266cd4e",
      "quote": "The pipeline ensures that only the training data is used when performing fit and the test data is used only for calculating the accuracy score"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "sha256:7e18c7e0f64d74a9396febd331e24a9f7b333170af2bb72bd837c16db266cd4e",
      "quote": "The pipeline can also be fed into a cross-validation function such as cross_val_score . Again, the pipeline ensures that the correct data subset and estimator method is used during fitting and predicting"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "answer",
  "answer": "The issue is data leakage because the entire dataset was transformed before splitting into train/test. A Pipeline should be used to chain feature selection and model estimators, ensuring only training data is used for fit and test data for prediction during cross-validation.",
  "abstention_reason": ""
}
